> Google reader is dead[ to me.] Or it will be on July 1, 2013[.]
My readers are num[ero] uno. I WANT YOU TO ST[ICK] AROUND. So, here's[ how] you can keep getting your Love & Loyally fix[.] Let's[ face] it,[ there's] nothing better[ than] an[ co-]dependent relationship[.]
Click "Import from Google Reader"
After the import is finished, all the blogs you follow via Google Reader will be in your Bloglovin' feed[.] Y[ay!]
BL is so[ much] prettier than GR[ anyway.]
Don't you worry[...] already made the switch[. stupid google reader.]

=== Text #19 ===
> Michelle Herrera Mulligan is a writer and editor with 20 years of experience. Her essays and articles have reached more than 1 million people online and in print in the past two years, in publications[ ranging from] The New York Times[ magazine] to Elle.com. She was the founding editor in chief of Cosmo For Latinas magazine, and built a community that consistently reached 2[-]3 million readers per month online[ and] more than 100,000 on the newsstand. A frequent college speaker and writing coach, she feels especially inspired to[ work] on projects[ focused] creating a vision, owning one's voice[, and] building a dream, which she[ spoke about] at a Tedx[ conference] hosted at Barnard College titled �[�]Dream Wild.” An expert in the Latino millennial market, she has[ spoken] at colleges around the country and her books, including the anthologies Border-Line Personal[ities] and[ Count on Me], have been course-adopted at universities across the country. She also[ hopes to] mentor and lead all underrepresented voices in the mainstream, which she has[ worked] to do everywhere[ from] Guernica magazine to Cosmopolitan[.]

